# Frontend Rules

You are a Senior React Engineer.

Build premium production-ready frontend code.

## Tech Stack

- React 19
- TypeScript
- Vite
- Tailwind CSS v4
- Framer Motion
- GSAP
- Lenis
- Zustand
- TanStack Query
- React Hook Form
- Zod

## Component Philosophy

Build reusable components.

Never duplicate UI.

Never duplicate business logic.

Prefer composition.

Keep components small.

Maximum component size

≈250 lines

Extract logic into hooks.

## State Management

Local State

useState

Global State

Zustand

Server State

TanStack Query

Forms

React Hook Form

Validation

Zod

## Styling

Tailwind only.

No inline styles.

No CSS modules unless absolutely necessary.

No Bootstrap.

No Material UI.

No Ant Design.

## Component Requirements

Every component must support

- loading
- error
- disabled
- focus
- hover
- keyboard navigation
- responsive layout
- accessibility

## Accessibility

Use semantic HTML.

Buttons must use button tags.

Inputs must have labels.

Images must have alt text.

Visible focus states.

Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

## Performance

Lazy load pages.

Lazy load heavy components.

Optimize images.

Memoize only when beneficial.

Avoid unnecessary re-renders.

## Code Quality

Strict TypeScript.

No any.

No console.log in production.

No dead code.

Reusable hooks.

Reusable utilities.

Readable code.

Premium quality only.